# {{project_name}}

Generated by the `automation-generation` skill (binding `playwright-java-testng`)
from the approved test cases with `Needs Automation = TRUE`. See
`../AutomationGeneration.md` for the case mapping, locators and validation.

## Prerequisites

- JDK {{java_level}} or newer (`java -version`), Maven 3.6+ (`mvn -v`)
- Network access to {{base_url}}

## Environment variables

| Name | Required | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `{{username_env_var}}` | yes | Login user name — never stored in the project |
| `{{password_env_var}}` | yes | Login password — never stored in the project |
| `QA_BASE_URL` | no | Entry point (default `{{base_url}}`) |
| `QA_BROWSER` | no | `chromium` (default), `firefox`, `webkit` |
| `QA_HEADLESS` | no | `true` (default) / `false` |
| `QA_TIMEOUT_MS` | no | Action and assertion timeout (default {{default_timeout_ms}}) |
| `QA_ARTIFACTS_DIR` | no | Evidence root (default `{{default_artifacts_dir}}`) |
| `QA_RUN_ID` | no | Run identifier used in evidence paths |

## Run from the command line (Claude Code)

PowerShell:

```
$env:{{username_env_var}} = "<value>"; $env:{{password_env_var}} = "<value>"
mvn -q test
```

bash:

```
export {{username_env_var}}=<value> {{password_env_var}}=<value>
mvn -q test
```

First run only: Playwright downloads its browsers automatically on first use
(or run `mvn exec:java -e -D exec.mainClass=com.microsoft.playwright.CLI -D exec.args="install chromium"`).

## Run from IntelliJ IDEA

1. File > Open > select this folder's `pom.xml` > Open as Project.
2. Run > Edit Configurations > **{{run_name}}** (shared in `.run/`): fill the two
   credential variables locally. Their values stay in your IDE workspace only.
3. Run **{{run_name}}**. TestNG runs `testng.xml`; this works in the Community edition.

## Results

Machine-readable results: `target/surefire-reports/`. Failure evidence
(screenshot, trace, step log): `{{default_artifacts_dir}}/<run-id>/<case-id>/`.
Open a trace with `mvn exec:java -e -D exec.mainClass=com.microsoft.playwright.CLI -D exec.args="show-trace <trace.zip>"`.
